          "text": "Clinical Indication  \nHistory of generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 30 and occurring approximately once per month. Etiology is categorized as immune. Seizures are drug-responsive. Current antiseizure medication is lacosamide.\n\nTechnique  \nRoutine scalp EEG was recorded using the international 10–20 system with standard bipolar and referential montages.\n\nFindings  \nNo interictal epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures were identified during this recording.\n\nImpression  \nRoutine EEG without epileptiform abnormalities or electrographic seizures. This recording does not independently establish seizure type or ictal localization; correlation with the clinical history is required.",
